A||||59||Cliff Pennock||About signatures||||4||
Z||000000||Cliff Pennock||09-28-2001||11:35 AM||||Some time ago I had put an announcement up ("A note about signatures") - which BTW - is still up on every section page, about pictures in signatures.<P>I <B>still</B> see <B>huge</B> signatures here and there as well (animated) banners used as links to websites.<P>Please be aware that this is <B>not</B> what the signature is meant for. If you want to link to a website, please do so using a text link. If you want to include an image in your signature, make sure it's not too big. If in doubt, please re-read the announcement again.<BR>||||reg||4
Z||000001||skitime||09-28-2001||01:56 PM||||Cliff could you give us a pixel size in height and width that would be a limit.  If we know that we could then adjust our signatures accordingly. What someone calls big might be called huge by someone else.  Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000002||Fiero5||09-28-2001||02:04 PM||||Some of them are very creative. I know I have done a few myself  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>But then, at least in my case, I try to guess how small I need to go and still retain the look and details and such.<BR>Some sort of guide as to pixels/inches, etc would help us a lot.<P>Thanks Cliff.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/icons/icon7.gif"> <P>Steve||||reg||6
Z||000003||Cliff Pennock||09-28-2001||02:28 PM||||A signature (picture <B>plus</B> text should not be higher than 95 pixels and not wider than 600 pixels. A height of 95 pixels is about 6 lines of text.<P>Ideally, a signature picture should be less than 400 pixels wide so that horizontal scrolling is not necessary for those that use lower resolution displays (like webtv).<P>I see posts with one line of text, but including the signature, it takes up one complete screen.<P>Take a look at this thread <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/010577.html" TARGET=_blank>here</A>. Some signatures are perfect, others are far from perfect and actually quite annoying. Can you tell which is which?||||reg||1
Z||000004||MinnGreenGT||09-28-2001||02:39 PM||||My sig is 4" wide at 72 pixels per inch... is this still considered too large- the image is web optimized and about 35k. And I assume that because the flag image is posted in the header, it only loads into the browser once correct?<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/grngtsig3.jpg">     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fullstaff.gif">   <BR>Medium Metallic Green 87 GT<BR>3.1L High Output<BR>4 Spd OD Tranny<BR>Open (read: Loud) Exhaust<BR>and More!<BR>-Rob Bartlett||||reg||1
Z||000005||Cliff Pennock||09-28-2001||02:44 PM||||MinnGreenGT, your picture is about right (although it could be a bit smaller but then I would be nitpicking  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> ) but including the text in your signature, it takes up a full screen on my system (800x600).||||reg||1
Z||000006||Fiero5||09-28-2001||02:45 PM||||I am assuming that the banner "www.fieroworld.com" is the one in question on that thread? All the others seem fine to me anyway.<P>Steve||||reg||5
Z||000007||mbramble||09-28-2001||02:49 PM||||Personally, I think you should just remove the option of posting image files with signatures.  This topic keeps coming up over and over and people still can't learn to: 1. make them an appropriate size and 2. not insert them for every post they make.  Some posts are nothing but the same people's signatures over and over.  If ya wanna show your Fiero off, post a picture some where and put a link to it in your signature.  If people <I>want</I> to look they can, if they don't care to see it, they aren't forced to by reading an otherwise useful or informative topic.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Phil||09-28-2001||02:51 PM||||I think Cliff means that the pic(if used)AND other info should be no larger than 6 lines of text, just using MinnGreenGT as an example - you have a pic PLUS 6 lines of text.(no flame intended)<P>------------------<BR> <BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_1.gif">   <BR>SC 3800||||reg||1
Z||000009||mbramble||09-28-2001||02:52 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Cliff Pennock:<BR><B>MinnGreenGT, your picture is about right (although it could be a bit smaller but then I would be nitpicking    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> ) but including the text in your signature, it takes up a full screen on my system (800x600).</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>My system is set for 1024x768 on a 17" monitor and that post takes up just a bit more that 1/2 of my browser window.  For a two line post.....<P>Not pickin on you Green, just pointing out how much space a typical signature takes up...<P><p>[This message has been edited by mbramble (edited 09-28-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000010||stimpy||09-28-2001||03:02 PM||||Trust me, they'll never learn. I think it's time to ditch the signatures altogether.||||reg||1
Z||000011||Cliff Pennock||09-28-2001||03:09 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Fiero5:<BR><B>I am assuming that the banner "www.fieroworld.com" is the one in question on that thread? All the others seem fine to me anyway.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>The banner is indeed not what the signature is meant for, even though its size is perfect. A text link would suffice and you could use a picture to show (off) your Fiero. Or use a picture of your Fiero as a link to your website.<P>But most of the signatures in that thread are too large.<P>Please be aware that this is not (only) a personal opinion. I still receive a lot of complaints about the use of signatures. I'm just trying to make the threads more readible.||||reg||1
Z||000012||MinnGreenGT||09-28-2001||03:32 PM||||Don't worry... I'm not taken any flames for this!  I posted my signature to get truthful opinions!  So Thanks!  I will try to shrink my signature in order not to suck up bandwith of those who aren't running big monitors (I'm either on a 17", 19", or 21") and high-speed connections (I'm usually on a DSL too).  I have always preferred honest opinions in opposition of suckups!<P>BTW: Cliff- you're awsome... keep up the great work!||||reg||1
Z||000013||skitime||09-28-2001||04:43 PM||||New shrunken signature. The pic is 400x 100 pixels though.  I am testing to see what it looks like.  <P>------------------<BR><UL TYPE=SQUARE><BR><LI>Red 88 GT T-TOP<BR><LI>Red 86 GT<BR></UL>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/signature-2.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000014||skitime||09-28-2001||04:48 PM||||Cliff, why does mine have the large space after the dotted line.  I don't see anything that would cause this and it is taking up a lot of space.<P><p>[This message has been edited by skitime (edited 09-28-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000015||CoolBlue87GT||09-28-2001||04:50 PM||||     <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Cliff Pennock:<BR>[B] I still receive a lot of complaints about the use of signatures. [B]<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>Cliff,<P>Question, Are WebTV users are complaining, or those with real computers ?  <P>I ask, because the page you posted looked fine. The MintGT was a little bigger than the rest, but I didn't mind.<P>I work at a RadioShack, and we stop selling WebTV's a long time ago. I don't remember the display size those had.<P>I use a laptop running Microsoft Explorer, Font is set to medium. Using a 56K modem(usually getting 49500bps line)<P>Is the display different/smaller on those WebTV's ?<P>Thanks for the info.<P>P.S.  Skitime, those look fine also.<BR><p>[This message has been edited by CoolBlue87GT (edited 09-28-2001).]||||reg||5
Z||000016||Jaygee79||09-28-2001||05:08 PM||||I know there's a way to make it so that nothing more than a specified size is allowed. That would be a quick and easy way of getting them down.<P>I know in my case, my pic is smaller in actual size than many others yet it is more bytes.  I can't figure out how to make it smaller.||||reg||1
Z||000017||MinnGreenGT||09-28-2001||05:18 PM||||Jaygee... if you have access to photoshop, use the "save for web" option.  Or reduce the quality value when you save as a JPG image.  Photoshop 5.5 & 6.0 also have a built in go-between with Adobe Image-Ready.  Another option would be to save it with an indexed color palette, but I never like the results of that.  Just play with it a bit... you'll get it down a ways.<P>BTW: I love AUS's & Tigger's signatures.  They look great and don't take up much space. They just look really clean.  I think I'll try to make mine similiar to theirs...||||reg||1
Z||000018||snafus87||09-28-2001||05:21 PM||||My system is set to 1280x1024 resolution on a 19" Trinitron monitor and I don't really have a problem with the SIZE of the signiatures, just the animated ones (read: My connection is lacking), they take a while to download over my modem.<P>------------------<BR>JT Krupa<BR>85 GT<BR>(fastback conversion)<BR>180+ K miles<BR>Lehighton, PA||||reg||1
