Z||000022||72vinman||09-28-2001||06:19 PM||||I think one of the things to remember is that you only need to show your signature in your first post of a thread. Please do not keep using you sig in every post.||||reg||1
Z||000023||Monkeyman||09-28-2001||06:36 PM||||Here are a couple of thoughts.  First, what about thumbnails?  Would that work?  Second, IE6 (sorry for saying the "IE" word, Cliff  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> ) has something that automatically loads the image to fit on the screen (I'm guessing to a certain size), then you can click on a little box that pops up and enlarge the pic to it's original size.  Click on the box again and it's back to it's smaller size.  I have no idea what this is called and I have no other info about it, but it's a neat idea.||||reg||1
Z||000024||Cliff Pennock||09-28-2001||06:42 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by CoolBlue87GT:<BR><B>Question, Are WebTV users are complaining, or those with real computers ?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Actually, I haven't had too many complaints from WebTV users since there aren't many out there. But please realize that most people (by far) are <B>still</B> surfing using a resolution of 800x600. And for those, the large signatures are very annoying (physical size wise). For those surfing the net using modems, the large signatures present another problem: download time.<P>Let me give an example (I took a random picture out of the gallery to illustrate this):<P><B>Wrong signature:</B><BR>--------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/wrong_signature.jpg"> <BR>Black Formula<BR>Mint Condition<BR>Only 76,000 miles!<BR>--------------------<P><B>Good signature (12K):</B><BR>---------------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/good_signature.jpg"> <BR>Black Formula, Mint Condition, Only 76,000 miles!<BR>---------------------------<P><B>Better signature (16K):</B><BR>---------------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/best_signature.gif"> <BR>---------------------------<P>I understand not everybody has PhotoShop, but there are a lot of freeware paint programs out there with which you can at least size and/or crop your image.||||reg||1
Z||000025||Cliff Pennock||09-28-2001||06:46 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Monkeyman:<BR><B>then you can click on a little box that pops up and enlarge the pic to it's original size. Click on the box again and it's back to it's smaller size.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Well, I've been thinking about something similar where all signatures would be replaced by a link to an enhanced profile (where you can show off your ride and share other information). Then again, I don't mind signatures at all, neither do most people because they actually add to the experience - if only we could keep them within reason.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000026||FLASHY||09-28-2001||07:39 PM||||First of all, I want to ask Cliff and everyone else if my new signature is ok? It is only 350 x 70 pixels and only 24 kb.<P>Second, I know some people say they have problems with animated signatures due to the slow download time but in this case the file size is smaller than many decent sized ones. So does that make it ok?<P>Third, I personally like when people add their signature every time because I quite often look for their symbol as I scroll down to see a particular person's response. It speeds up the searching process for me. PLUS I'm a VERY visual person so I can tie signatures with someone a lot better than just their name. If their signature is sometimes there and sometimes not it gets a little confusing (and I know that's my problem but I'm telling you my opinion). I know that bothers a lot of you but I'm showing there are some who like it the other way too.<P>Thanks for reading my reply.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/spinsig3.gif">  <p>[This message has been edited by FLASHY (edited 09-28-2001).]||||reg||1
